    {
      "v": 2,
      "zh": "我立刻被圣灵感动，见有一个宝座安置在天上，又有一位坐在宝座上。",
      "en": "Immediately I was in the Spirit,[NOTE:1] and[NOTE:2] a throne was standing[NOTE:3] in heaven with someone seated on it!",
      "notes": [
        "Or “in the spirit.” “Spirit” could refer either to the Holy Spirit or the human spirit, but in either case John was in “a state of spiritual exaltation best described as a trance” (R. H. Mounce, Revelation [NICNT], 75).",
        "Grk “and behold.” The Greek word ἰδού (idou) at the beginning of this statement has not been translated because it has no exact English equivalent here, but adds interest and emphasis (BDAG 468 s.v. 1).",
        "BDAG 537 s.v. κεῖμαι 2 gives the translation “stand” for the term in this verse."
