    {
      "v": 6,
      "zh": "宝座前好像一个玻璃海，如同水晶。宝座中和宝座周围有四个活物，前后遍体都满了眼睛。",
      "en": "and in front of the throne was something like a sea of glass, like crystal.[NOTE:1] In[NOTE:2] the middle of the throne[NOTE:3] and around the throne were four living creatures[NOTE:4] full of eyes in front and in back.",
      "notes": [
        "This could refer to rock crystal, but it is possible this refers to ice (an older meaning). See BDAG 571 s.v. κρύσταλλος.",
        "Here καί (kai) has not been translated because of differences between Greek and English style.",
        "Perhaps, “in the middle of the throne area” (see L&N 83.10).",
        "On the meaning of ζῴον (zōon) BDAG 431 s.v. 2 states, “Of the four peculiar beings at God’s throne, whose description Rv 4:6-9 reminds one of the ζῷα in Ezk 1:5ff, the cherubim. S. also Rv 5:6, 8, 11, 14; 6:1, 3, 5-7; 7:11; 14:3; 15:7; 19:4.”"
      ],
